\s1 Ruth’s Redemption Assured
\p \v 1 \w One day Ruth’s mother-in-law|strong="H2545"\w* \w Naomi|strong="H5281"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* to her, “\w My daughter|strong="H1323"\w*, \w should I not|strong="H3808"\w* \w seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w a resting place|strong="H4494"\w* for you, \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w it may be well|strong="H3190"\w* with you? \v 2 \w Now|strong="H6258"\w* \w is not|strong="H3808"\w* \w Boaz|strong="H1162"\w*, \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w whose|strong="H834"\w* \w servant girls|strong="H5291"\w* \w you have been working|strong="H1961"\w*, \w a relative of ours|strong="H4130"\w*? \w In fact|strong="H2009"\w*, \w tonight|strong="H3915"\w* \w he|strong="H1931"\w* \w is winnowing|strong="H2219"\w* \w barley|strong="H8184"\w* \w on the threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w*. \v 3 \w Therefore wash yourself|strong="H7364"\w*, \w put on perfume|strong="H5480"\w*, \w and wear|strong="H7760"\w* \w your best clothes|strong="H8071"\w*. \w Go down|strong="H3381"\w* \w to the threshing floor|strong="H1637"\w*, \w but do not|strong="H408"\w* \w let the man|strong="H376"\w* \w know|strong="H3045"\w* \w you are there until|strong="H5704"\w* \w he has finished|strong="H3615"\w* \w eating|strong="H398"\w* \w and drinking|strong="H8354"\w*. \v 4 \w When he lies down|strong="H7901"\w*, \w note|strong="H3045"\w* \w the place|strong="H4725"\w* \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w he lies|strong="H7901"\w*. \w Then go in|strong="H935"\w* \w and uncover|strong="H1540"\w* \w his feet|strong="H4772"\w*, \w and lie down|strong="H7901"\w*, \w and he|strong="H1931"\w* \w will explain|strong="H5046"\w* to you \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w you should do|strong="H6213"\w*.”
