\p \v 16 \w When Ruth returned|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w her mother-in-law|strong="H2545"\w*, \w Naomi asked her|strong="H559"\w*, “\w How did it go|strong="H4310"\w*, \w my daughter|strong="H1323"\w*?”
\p \w Then Ruth told|strong="H5046"\w* her \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Boaz|strong="H376"\w* \w had done|strong="H6213"\w* for her. \v 17 \w And she said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w He gave|strong="H5414"\w* me \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w six|strong="H8337"\w* \w measures of barley|strong="H8184"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w he said|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w go back|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w your mother-in-law|strong="H2545"\w* \w empty-handed|strong="H7387"\w*.’”
