\s1 The Line of David
\r (\ref Matthew 1:1–17|MAT 1:1-17\ref*; \ref Luke 3:23–38|LUK 3:23-38\ref*)
\p \v 18 \w Now these are|strong="H428"\w* \w the generations|strong="H8435"\w* \w of Perez|strong="H6557"\w*:
\b 
\li1 \w Perez|strong="H6557"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Hezron|strong="H2696"\w*,
\li1 \v 19 \w Hezron|strong="H2696"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Ram|strong="H7410"\w*,
\li1 \w Ram|strong="H7410"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Amminadab|strong="H5992"\w*,
\li1 \v 20 \w Amminadab|strong="H5992"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Nahshon|strong="H5177"\w*,
\li1 \w Nahshon|strong="H5177"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Salmon|strong="H8009"\w*,\f + \fr 4:20 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts, some LXX manuscripts, and Vulgate (see also verse 21 and LXX of \ref 1 Chronicles 2:11|1CH 2:11\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Salma\f*
\li1 \v 21 \w Salmon|strong="H8012"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Boaz|strong="H1162"\w*,
\li1 \w Boaz|strong="H1162"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Obed|strong="H5744"\w*,
\li1 \v 22 \w Obed|strong="H5744"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w Jesse|strong="H3448"\w*,
\li1 \w and Jesse|strong="H3448"\w* \w was the father of|strong="H3205"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*.
